<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks rise.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks rise.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			17/7/97		  10/7/97	     19/7/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	425-450		  375-400	     400-425</p>
<p>    Naphtha	     100		   75-100		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,900		    1,850		 1,450</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	325-350			300		   425</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     15			 15		    15</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks rose with incoming components and finished product. Some barges left for Germany, but there were few outward cargo movements.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks rose slightly with arriving cargoes.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks went up as cargoes arrived from Russia and the Med. Barges exited down the Rhine, but little left by cargo.</p>
<p>Fuel oil inventories also gained with the arrival of straight-run and cracked cargoes and some departure of cracked material to the bunker market.</p>
<p>Jet fuel levels were steady.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
</text>
